"}
{"abstract":"Wildfires, exacerbated by climate extremes, pose escalating global threats. Despite advancements in technology, current wildfire management policies lack specific details a bout integrated management and stakeholder engagement. This study provides empirical evidence on how five European wildfire management locations align with networked governance models by analyzing how their stakeholder networks a re configured through social network analysis (SNA). This is measured by assessing network configuration and stakeholder group profiles. Measurements at the network level assess the size, density, diversity of sectors, scalar levels of operation, and phases. At stakeholder level, relevance is assessed by measuring in degree, eccentricity, closeness centrality, and betweenness centrality. Analysis qualitatively assesses the network profile, leading to the discussion on the primary factors influencing network configurations and the potential outcomes of these attributes.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Vallim, Diogo","Giannakopoulou, Amalia","Schmid, Anna","Struthers, David","Altsitsiadis, Efthymios","Fróes, Isabel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-808915"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Climate extremes","Networked governance","Social network analysis","Stakeholder engagement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"networks for integrated wildfire management a social network analysis approach","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.59297/1kbr4158","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-808915","identifier":[{"id":"85209184238","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7dd21677-7ec8-4b14-a928-99346bd4686c"],"keyword":["Climate extremes","Networked governance","Social network analysis","Stakeholder engagement","Wildfire management"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-427A8FBAB7CF87B7EC0C9E7D3B216AFB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.59297/1kbr4158","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Diogo","key":"vallimpau","last":"Vallim","name":"Vallim, Diogo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amalia","key":"giannakopouloupau","last":"Giannakopoulou","name":"Giannakopoulou, Amalia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"schmidpau","last":"Schmid","name":"Schmid, Anna","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"strutherspau","last":"Struthers","name":"Struthers, David","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Efthymios","key":"altsitsiadispau","last":"Altsitsiadis","name":"Altsitsiadis, Efthymios","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Isabel","key":"fróespau","last":"Fróes","name":"Fróes, Isabel","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-7dd21677-7ec8-4b14-a928-99346bd4686c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Networks for Integrated Wildfire Management: A Social Network Analysis Approach","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-808915","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This article presents a case that joins user-driven innovation and Additive manufacturing (AM) towards latent business opportunities in the preparation for life threatening operations. Surgeons, confronted with a patient with a delicate heart condition, collaborated with a prototyping facility to print a realistic 3D model of the patient’s aortic aneurysm. The model allowed the surgeons to first study and then experiment to determine the most effective operation procedure before the actual operation, which shortened the surgery time by approximately 70%. Reducing surgery time creates two forms of value: improving patient outcomes and reducing costs. Shorter times under anesthetic and on cardiopulmonary bypass correlate with better surgical results. Reducing healthcare costs brings broad societal benefits in both publicly and privately funded healthcare systems. We outline a case for makerspaces to capture value by joining their expertise and manufacturing equipment with the needs of nearby healthcare systems for novel business developments.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Fróes, Isabel","Struthers, David M.","Malacarne, Ciro","Perini, Matteo","Rossi, Maurizio","Gregori, Paolo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-688550"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Fróes, Isabel"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Trentino Sviluppo SPA"],"keyword":["Additive manufacturing","Business","Healthcare","Interdisciplinary","Makerspaces","User driven innovation"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the beating heart of untapped business opportunities for additive manufacturing","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.12688/openreseurope.16270.1","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["First version published online 7 September 2023. Second version published 05 July 2024."],"id":"S01-000.00-688550","identifier":[{"id":"85198218795","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-7eccb579-36c1-46dc-be21-366733820f10"],"keyword":["Additive manufacturing","Business","Healthcare","Interdisciplinary","Makerspaces","User-driven innovation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E572CA8DF24F8138B43BC7ED3B37A63F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.12688/openreseurope.16270.1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/106535516/30f97455-60df-40f5-ab1e-9048a185ae63_16270_-_isabel_froes_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/96685765/isabel_froes_et_al_the_beating_heart_of_untapped_business_opportunities_for_additive_manufacturing_version_1_awaiting_peer_review.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.12688/openreseurope.16270.2","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Society and Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"trentino sviluppo spa","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Trentino Sviluppo SPA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Isabel","key":"fróespau","last":"Fróes","locid":"2f70c270-cadd-4849-854c-70495ec28c58","name":"Fróes, Isabel","orcid":"0000-0001-8199-2440","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David M.","key":"strutherspau","last":"Struthers","name":"Struthers, David M.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ciro","key":"malacarnepau","last":"Malacarne","name":"Malacarne, Ciro","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Matteo","key":"perinipau","last":"Perini","name":"Perini, Matteo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maurizio","key":"rossipau","last":"Rossi","name":"Rossi, Maurizio","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"gregoripau","last":"Gregori","name":"Gregori, Paolo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.12688/openreseurope.16270.1","issn":["27325121"],"journal":"Open Research Europe","paperid":"143","publisher":"European Commission","status":"p","title":"Open Research Europe","volume":"3"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198218795"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-7eccb579-36c1-46dc-be21-366733820f10"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"The Beating Heart of Untapped Business Opportunities for Additive Manufacturing","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-688550","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Denmark’s private non-profit housing (almene boliger) sector provides affordable housing and social housing and is capable of being self-governing and self-financing. We examine the private non-profit housing sector’s governance and financing model and assess the extent to which its institutional framework and revolving funds model allow it to serve as a role model for the development of affordable housing in other countries and cities. The paper concludes that while Denmark’s private non-profit housing system has succeeded in providing affordable housing with relatively low levels of public financing, its exposure to state intervention risks weakening its governance and financial power.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Noring, Luise","Struthers, David","Grydehøj, Adam"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-279465"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Grydehøj, Adam"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Guangzhou University"],"keyword":["Affordable housing","Copenhagen","Denmark","Financing","Governance","Housing policy","Urban"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["City Facilitators"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"governing and financing affordable housing at the intersection of the market and the state denmark s private non profit housing system","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/65910747/luise_noring_et_al_governing_and_financing_affordable_housing_acceptedmanuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Because the bulk of rental payments go to the National Building Foundation once the mortgages and subsidies have been paid off, the National Building Foundation’s savings increase as the private non-profit housing stock ages, providing the system with the financial basis for funding new housing in the future. In 2007, post-mortgage payments of DKK 229 million (US$36 million) were made into the National Building Foundation, a sum that is expected to rise to around DKK 3 billion (US$470 million) by 2020 and DKK 3.4 billion (US$530 million) by 2030 (KAB 2016 ). This massive increase in contributions over time reflects the aging of the housing estates and hence the repayments of mortgages and subsidies, yet it also coincides with a rising need for costly renovations and replacement. Danish municipalities likewise place money in the National Building Foundation to cover loans for developing new private non-profit housing."],"id":"S01-000.00-279465","identifier":[{"id":"85089088168","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-2b2741cf-86c0-4500-a636-0143229c7444"],"keyword":["Affordable housing","Copenhagen","Denmark","Financing","Governance","Housing policy","Urban"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-96D052130B9E1A6AE4DFEF88D17600D1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/65910747/luise_noring_et_al_governing_and_financing_affordable_housing_acceptedmanuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Society and Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"guangzhou university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Guangzhou University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["City Facilitators"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luise","key":"noringpau","last":"Noring","locid":"c019e668-658b-424e-b19e-c1a50d068dc8","name":"Noring, Luise","orcid":"0000-0002-0383-1382","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"strutherspau","last":"Struthers","name":"Struthers, David","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Adam","key":"grydehøjpau","last":"Grydehøj","name":"Grydehøj, Adam","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/17535069.2020.1798495","issn":["17535069","17535077"],"issn_org":["17535069"],"issue":"2","journal":"Urban Research & Practice","pages":"258-274","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Urban Research & Practice","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089088168"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-2b2741cf-86c0-4500-a636-0143229c7444"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Governing and Financing Affordable Housing at the Intersection of the Market and the State : Denmark’s Private Non-profit Housing System","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-279465","year":"2022","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This article explores the mutual influence between a city government’s jurisdictional capacity (its ability to plan and implement policy) and its interactions with other governance actors. It does so by quantifying, categorizing, and analyzing the composition of governance actors at various levels (national, regional, local) and of various types (public, private, civic) that are active in large-scale urban development projects in three cities: Hamburg, Manchester, Pittsburgh. Considering these findings in the context of national governance infrastructures, the article argues that divergent arrays of jurisdictional capacity (linked to multilevel distributions of state power) influence how city governments engage with other governance actors and influence which governance actors they engage with. This not only impacts project outcomes but also ultimately reinforces the kinds of governance strategies in which cities engage.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Noring, Luise","Ohler, Laura Prisca","Struthers, David"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-294814"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Noring, Luise"],"keyword":["City government","Governance","Infrastructure","Project governance","Urban development"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["City Facilitators"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"city government capacity and patterns in urban development project governance","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/65910728/luise_noring_et_al_city_government_capacity_acceptedmanuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-294814","identifier":[{"id":"000509646900001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85078785474","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-cc20adc7-4558-45d2-8849-4e3b25607958"],"keyword":["City government","Governance","Infrastructure","Project governance","Urban development"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-418BC5976DAA0158C46B8023147C6AD5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/65910728/luise_noring_et_al_city_government_capacity_acceptedmanuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Society and Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["City Facilitators"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luise","key":"noringpau","last":"Noring","locid":"c019e668-658b-424e-b19e-c1a50d068dc8","name":"Noring, Luise","orcid":"0000-0002-0383-1382","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura Prisca","key":"ohlerpau","last":"Ohler","name":"Ohler, Laura Prisca","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"strutherspau","last":"Struthers","name":"Struthers, David","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/1078087419897808","issn":["10780874","15528332"],"issn_org":["10780874"],"issue":"5","journal":"Urban Affairs Review","pages":"1343-1371","publisher":"SAGE Publications Inc.","status":"p","title":"Urban Affairs Review","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85078785474"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-cc20adc7-4558-45d2-8849-4e3b25607958"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"City Government Capacity and Patterns in Urban Development Project Governance","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-294814","year":"2021","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Social media data are increasingly used to study a variety of social phenomena. This development is based on the assumption that digital traces left on social media can provide insights into the nature of human interaction. In this research, we turn our attention to what remains invisible in research based on social media data. Using Andrea Brighenti’s work on ‘social visibility’ as a point of departure, we unpack data invisibilities, as they are created within four dimensions: people and intentionality, technologies and tools, accessibility and form, and meaning and imaginaries. We introduce the notion of quasi-visible data as an intermediary between visible and invisible data highlighting the processual character of data invisibilities. With this conceptual framework we contribute to developing a more reflective and ethical field of research into the study of social phenomena based on social media data. We conclude by arguing that distancing ourselves from the assumption that all social media data are visible and focusing on the invisible will enhance our understanding of digital data.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Neumayer, Christina","Rossi, Luca","Struthers, David M."],"cuid":["S02-093.23-038290"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Computational methods","Digital Methods","Epistemology","Social media data","Visibilities"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"invisible data a framework for understanding visibility processes in social media data","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/205630