","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This chapter explores the materialities of social media as archives of social movements’ user-generated content. By conceptualizing social media as archives, we unpack how the materiality of social media shapes production and storage of mediated communication by social movements resulting in processes of over- and under-representation. These processes are not controlled by activists, but largely by social media logics. The loss of control over their own data leads to social movements’ practices of avoidance, which might result in invisibilities and incomplete archives. We conclude by arguing that inclusive archiving projects of social movements’ mediated communication and writing a history from below in social media should rather be non-commercial projects in close collaboration with activists. Writing a history from below by creating archives where activists lay claim to their own representation and regain control over their data is understood as a way to make visible imbalances of power.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Neumayer, Christina","Struthers, David"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382307"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Inclusive Archiving","Materiality of Social Media","Social Media Archives","Social movements","User generated content"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"social media as activist archives","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.routledge.com/Social-Media-Materialities-and-Protest-Critical-Reflections-1st-Edition/Mortensen-Neumayer-Poell/p/book/9781138093089","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382307","ids":["itu-45ebf867-cf8b-4928-bf9c-fb9147726aa5"],"keyword":["Inclusive Archiving","Materiality of Social Media","Social Media Archives","Social Movements","User-Generated Content"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4E89B5D87D7C4E0413D5CD12CF96E28F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"neumayerpau","last":"Neumayer","name":"Neumayer, Christina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"strutherspau","last":"Struthers","name":"Struthers, David","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mette","key":"mortensenpedh","last":"Mortensen","name":"Mortensen, Mette","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Christina","key":"neumayerpedh","last":"Neumayer","name":"Neumayer, Christina","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"poellpedh","last":"Poell","name":"Poell, Thomas","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781351605984"],"pages":"86-98","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Social Media Materialities and Protest: Critical Reflections"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-45ebf867-cf8b-4928-bf9c-fb9147726aa5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Social Media as Activist Archives","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382307","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
